# Answer

Put the answer in the first paragraph. Use an answer page for one narrow question, so a reader can stop after the opening paragraph and still have what they need. The shared limits for every page template are on [Page templates](index.html).

## When to use it

Use it for a small household or documentation question, such as the difference between a theme colour and a display mode. Give the answer first, then the essential context, then a link to the relevant setting or detailed guide. If the question needs several steps, use a [guide](guide.html) or [detailed guide](detailed-guide.html) instead.

## Structure and behaviour

Use one descriptive title, a concise answer, optional supporting headings and a small group of related links. Write link text that names the destination ([WG-083](../../content/writing-guidelines/add-links.html#wg-083)). Keep live values out of permanent prose unless the page reads and labels the current state. A page about a setting must not read as if the reader has changed it.

## Home Assistant boundary

An answer page is reference content. It does not add a Home Assistant panel, and it does not stand in for a device's current state. Do not add a promotional or feedback form unless it has a real purpose and endpoint.

